\title{RGenEDA: Genomic Exploratory Data Analysis}
\description{
RGenEDA collects the plots and summaries that are repeated in most bulk
RNA-seq exploratory data analyses (EDA), built around the DESeq2 workflow,
into one S4 object, \code{geneda}, and a set of functions that work on it.
}
\section{Typical workflow}{

\enumerate{
\item Build a \code{geneda} object with \code{\link[=GenEDA]{GenEDA()}} (from matrices) or
\code{\link[=as.geneda]{as.geneda()}} (from a \code{SummarizedExperiment}, \code{DESeqDataSet} or
\code{DESeqTransform}).
\item Check the data with \code{\link[=PlotCountDist]{PlotCountDist()}}, \code{\link[=PlotDistances]{PlotDistances()}} and
\code{\link[=PlotHVGVariance]{PlotHVGVariance()}}.
\item Select highly variable genes with \code{\link[=FindVariableFeatures]{FindVariableFeatures()}} and run
PCA with \code{\link[=RunPCA]{RunPCA()}}. Explore it with \code{\link[=PlotScree]{PlotScree()}}, \code{\link[=PlotPCA]{PlotPCA()}},
\code{\link[=extractEigen]{extractEigen()}}, \code{\link[=PlotEigenHeatmap]{PlotEigenHeatmap()}} and \code{\link[=PlotEigenCorr]{PlotEigenCorr()}}; use
\code{\link[=PlotOrdCorr]{PlotOrdCorr()}} for NMDS ordination instead of PCA.
\item Store differential expression results with \code{\link[=SetDEGs]{SetDEGs()}}, filter them
with \code{\link[=FilterDEGs]{FilterDEGs()}} and \code{\link[=FindHVDEGs]{FindHVDEGs()}}, and plot them with \code{\link[=PlotMA]{PlotMA()}},
\code{\link[=PlotVolcano]{PlotVolcano()}}, \code{\link[=PlotPValHist]{PlotPValHist()}} or \code{\link[=DEDashboard]{DEDashboard()}}.
\item Save heatmaps with \code{\link[=GenSave]{GenSave()}}.
}

